      "math_academy_id": "q-145108",
      "sequence_position": 11,
      "problem": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following conditional probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2y+x}{4y+2}, & \\,0<x<2,\\,0<y<1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(\\frac{1}{4}<X<Y\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{3}{4}).$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n$$\nP(X\\in A\\,|\\,Y=y)={\\int }_{A}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ is the conditional probability density function of $X$ given $Y=y.$ \n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\frac{1}{4}<X<Y\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{3}{4}) & ={\\int }_{1/4}^{y}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y=\\frac{3}{4})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/4}^{3/4}\\frac{(2\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}+x)}{(4\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}+2)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{1/4}^{3/4}(x+\\frac{3}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{3x}{2}]}_{1/4}^{3/4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[{x}^{2}+3x]_{1/4}^{3/4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}({(\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}+3(\\frac{3}{4})-{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}-3(\\frac{1}{4})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}(\\frac{9}{16}+\\frac{9}{4}-\\frac{1}{16}-\\frac{3}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
      "result": "Correct",
